nodecode-dsers is a rewrite of dsers's dsers/dsers-agent-plugin:

  https://github.com/dsers/dsers-agent-plugin
  commit 58174bb9d9fdd8941eda76a9b898424852c6407e
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 DSers (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the original is a portable Agent Plugin package — a
plugin.json that marks the remote server untrusted, an mcp.json naming the
DSers MCP endpoint (https://ai.dsers.com/mcp), and eight Markdown skills
describing DSers's daily work (account and stores, product sourcing,
listing editing, product publishing, profit and pricing, supplier mapping,
order fulfillment, package tracking). The connection is now two Common Lisp
verbs, DSERS-TOOLS and DSERS-CALL, speaking the same protocol to the same
endpoint with the account's own access token; the eight skills are
condensed into the /dsers manual topic and one short standing note, which
carry their ground rules — read before writing, show what will change, wait
for a yes, never invent an id or a price, and what each DSers error code
means.

What was left out and why: the OAuth browser sign-in (the token is supplied
in the config section, as the cell does not run a web flow), the Agent
Plugin packaging and its untrusted-server call policy (Nodecode's own tool
approval covers that), and the eight skills' long reference files (order
blockers, pricing rules and legal references) — the manual topic keeps the
workflow and the guardrails, not the full prose.
